00:40.652 --> 00:43.334
then it crosses zero and
becomes slightly positive,

00:43.334 --> 00:45.651
more positive, even more positive.

00:45.651 --> 00:48.432
So you can see the slope
is constantly increasing.

00:48.432 --> 00:50.714
And if you think about it
in terms of derivatives,

00:50.714 --> 00:53.981
it means that you're first
derivative is increasing

00:53.981 --> 00:55.192
over that interval.

00:55.192 --> 00:57.218
And in order for your first
derivative to be increasing

00:57.218 --> 00:59.828
over that interval, your second derivative

00:59.828 --> 01:02.979
f prime prime of x, actually
let me write it as g,

01:02.979 --> 01:04.693
because we're using g in this example.

01:04.693 --> 01:08.002
In order for your first
derivative to be increasing,

01:08.002 --> 01:09.510
your, let me write this.

01:09.510 --> 01:10.343
So g,

01:11.578 --> 01:13.988
so concave upward means

01:13.988 --> 01:17.274
that your first derivative increasing,

01:17.274 --> 01:19.019
increasing,

01:19.019 --> 01:22.850
which means, which means
that your second derivative

01:22.850 --> 01:25.409
is greater than zero.

01:25.409 --> 01:28.325
And concave downward is the opposite.

01:28.325 --> 01:29.742
Concave downward,

01:32.728 --> 01:33.921
downward,

01:33.921 --> 01:36.463
is an interval, or you're
gonna be concave downward

01:36.463 --> 01:40.380
over an interval when
your slope is decreasing.

01:41.428 --> 01:44.095
